# <type>(<scope>): <subject>            <-- max ~72 chars; scope is optional
#
# Body: what & why (not how). Wrap at ~72. Blank line above.
#
# Footer: BREAKING CHANGE: ..., or issue refs like "Refs: JIRA-123".
#
# ── Conventional Commits (enforced by .githooks/commit-msg) ─────────────────
# type:  feat     new feature
#        fix      bug fix
#        docs     documentation only
#        style    formatting / whitespace (no code change)
#        refactor code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#        perf     performance improvement
#        test     adding or fixing tests
#        build    build system, dependencies, pom.xml
#        ci       CI configuration
#        chore    tooling / housekeeping
#        revert   reverts a previous commit
#
# Add "!" after type/scope for a breaking change, e.g.  feat(home)!: ...
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
